# Schoolhouse Gate, Noon Interval.
# Mrs. Teague: mother of two pupils, resident of Upper Ridge; defensive respectability.
NPC: school_parent
LOCATION: business_district
SCHEDULE: morning=upper_house_3, midday=schoolhouse_gate, evening=upper_house_3, night=upper_house_3

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(school_parent, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: parent_plain
  VOICE: violin_neutral_short_v1
  MRS. TEAGUE: "The children will be out in five minutes."
  [She pulls her wool shawl tighter against the harbor breeze, watching the schoolhouse doors.]
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v2
  MRS. TEAGUE: "I don't care to have men loitering by the railing while classes let out, mister."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(school_parent, default)
  TAG: parent_badge
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MRS. TEAGUE: "Officer Corwin. I hope you're not here to question the little ones about the estate."
  WALTER CORWIN: "I'm looking for anyone who saw visitors in town."
  VOICE: violin_questioning_medium_v1
  MRS. TEAGUE: "Visitors? This town has people who live here and people who ought not to be here.\nThat isn't complicated."

TOPIC: the_stranger_woman
  GATE: evidence(naomi)
  TAG: parent_naomi_sighting
  LABEL: "Ask if she saw Naomi Freeman and her boy"
  TIME: 7
  WALTER CORWIN: "You walk down from the ridge past the boardinghouse every noon.\nDid you see the colored woman and her son?"
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v2
  MRS. TEAGUE: "I saw them sitting on the low wall by the apothecary three mornings running."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Did they speak to anyone?"
  VOICE: violin_conspiratorial_long_v2
  MRS. TEAGUE: "The boy had a pocketful of smooth beach pebbles. He was lining them up in rows on the coping stones.\nMethodical little thing. Counting them in whisper."
  WALTER CORWIN: "And the mother?"
  VOICE: violin_neutral_long_v2
  MRS. TEAGUE: "She had an envelope tucked in her glove. Heavy paper, folded into four.\nShe didn't ask for charity. That's what bothered people, if you want the honest truth."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Why would that bother anyone?"
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_long_v1
  MRS. TEAGUE: "Because a pauper asks, and you give them two pennies or you don't, and the matter is settled.\nShe walked like someone who had come to collect what was already hers. That makes people nervous, Officer."
  NOTEBOOK: parent_naomi_attitude | "Mrs. Teague: Naomi Freeman 'walked like someone who had come to collect what was already hers. That makes people nervous.'"
  EVIDENCE: naomi_unapologetic_presence

TOPIC: the_estate_talk
  GATE: evidence(naomi)
  TAG: parent_estate_rumor
  LABEL: "Ask what the ridge families are saying about the club deaths"
  TIME: 7
  FORK:
    CHOICE: "Ask about Judge Wexford."
      VOICE: violin_neutral_long_v2
      MRS. TEAGUE: "Wexford was a stern magistrate. My husband sat on three grand juries with him.\nPeople say it was foul gas from the lower furnace pipes, but I know what Judge Wexford's housemaid found last Sunday."
      WALTER CORWIN: "What did she find?"
      VOICE: violin_neutral_long_v2
      MRS. TEAGUE: "Every mirror in the entry hall turned with its glass to the wall. And thirty pounds of coarse sea salt swept under the parlor rug.\nShe quit her place because she found the Judge sleeping upright in his library armchair with his boots tied together at the laces."
      WALTER CORWIN: "Tied together?"
      VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v1
      MRS. TEAGUE: "Knotted with heavy hemp, Officer. So he wouldn't sleepwalk toward the cliff in the dark."
      NOTEBOOK: parent_wexford_mirrors | "Judge Wexford's housemaid quit after finding mirrors turned to the wall, 30 lbs of salt under carpets, and Wexford sleeping upright with boots tied together to prevent sleepwalking to the cliff."
      EVIDENCE: turned_mirrors
      OUTCOME: estate_rumor_response = judge_wexford
    CHOICE: "Ask about Dr. Fenn."
      VOICE: violin_angry_long_v1
      MRS. TEAGUE: "Dr. Fenn delivered both my boys. A gentleman, though he grew peculiar after his sister passed.\nHe wouldn't prescribe camphor anymore. Said the smell 'attracted things from the cellar.'\nWe thought it was his age."
      NOTEBOOK: parent_fenn_peculiar | "Dr. Fenn stopped prescribing camphor, claiming the odor 'attracted things from the cellar.'"
      EVIDENCE: fenn_camphor_taboo
      OUTCOME: estate_rumor_response = doctor_fenn

# Redundant-carrier backup: if schoolteacher is missed, this supplies the
# same EVIDENCE the covering-letter lead relies on downstream.
TOPIC: the_covering_letter
  GATE: evidence(curriculum_abridgment) AND NOT evidence(reader_omission_letter)
  TAG: parent_covering_letter
  LABEL: "Ask if she recalls the covering letter approving the reader"
  TIME: 5
  WALTER CORWIN: "Mr. Abernathy says the school committee approved a letter cutting the crew list from the reader."
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v2
  MRS. TEAGUE: "My husband sits on that committee, Officer. He read it aloud at the Tuesday meeting, proud as anything."
  [She recites from memory, counting the words off on gloved fingers.]
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_long_v1
  MRS. TEAGUE: "'Retain the subscriptions toward rebuilding. Omit the accompanying crew list from the school edition. Approved by the committee.' Signed by Mr. Abernathy himself."
  WALTER CORWIN: "You remember it word for word."
  VOICE: violin_conspiratorial_medium_v1
  MRS. TEAGUE: "A woman remembers exactly the sentence that decided what her own children would and wouldn't be taught, Officer."
  NOTEBOOK: parent_covering_letter_1 | "Mrs. Teague recites the committee's covering letter from memory, matching Hallowell's copy word for word: rebuilding subscriptions retained, crew list omitted, approved and signed by Abernathy."
  EVIDENCE: reader_omission_letter

# Redundant-carrier backup: if schoolteacher is missed, this supplies the
# same EVIDENCE the sanitized-textbook lead relies on downstream.
TOPIC: the_reader_lesson
  GATE: NOT evidence(sanitized_textbook)
  TAG: parent_reader_lesson
  LABEL: "Ask what her children recite about the 1823 disaster"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "What does the school reader teach about the Ophion?"
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v1
  MRS. TEAGUE: "My youngest recites it every Friday for penmanship practice."
  [She straightens, reciting in the flat cadence of a memorized lesson.]
  VOICE: violin_haunting_medium_v2
  MRS. TEAGUE: "'The sea received its harvest, and Christian fortitude and the generosity of our founding estates preserved Widow's Bight from ruin.' Chapter Four, page twelve. She's copied it into her fair-hand book twice."
  NOTEBOOK: parent_reader_lesson_1 | "Mrs. Teague's daughter recites the school reader's Chapter Four passage from memory: 'The sea received its harvest... founding estates preserved Widow's Bight from ruin.'"
  EVIDENCE: sanitized_textbook

# Redundant-carrier backup: if post_office_clerk is missed, this supplies the
# same EVIDENCE the New Bedford letters lead relies on downstream, building
# on Mrs. Teague's own already-established sighting of the envelope.
TOPIC: the_new_bedford_letters
  GATE: evidence(naomi_unapologetic_presence) AND NOT evidence(new_bedford_letters)
  TAG: parent_new_bedford_letters
  LABEL: "Ask what she noticed about the envelope Naomi carried"
  TIME: 5
  WALTER CORWIN: "You said Naomi Freeman had an envelope tucked in her glove. Did you see where it was from?"
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v2
  MRS. TEAGUE: "I don't make a habit of reading other women's post, Officer. But she wasn't discreet about it, not entirely."
  [She adjusts her shawl, remembering.]
  VOICE: violin_conspiratorial_long_v1
  MRS. TEAGUE: "She told the boy, plain as anything, that his brother's letter had come again from the mission in New Bedford.\nSaid he'd have his answer once she'd 'collected what was owed.' I assumed she meant charity. I understand now she didn't."
  NOTEBOOK: parent_new_bedford_letters_1 | "Mrs. Teague overheard Naomi tell her son a letter had arrived again from the New Bedford mission, and that he'd have his answer once she'd 'collected what was owed.'"
  EVIDENCE: new_bedford_letters
